# Core rules

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). This is team Martian Mappers' NASA Space Apps 2026 repo (`nasathingamajig`).

- **No application code and no project data pipeline before 14 November 2026.** Do not add `.py`, `.js`, `.ts`, notebooks, or `package.json` dependency installs until then. Documentation, tool installs, and role decisions are fine. Starting the build early may disqualify the team. Confirm in the Project Submission Guide (expected 13 November).
- **No secrets.** Never commit `.env`, API keys, tokens, or credentials. The NASA API key exists only as the environment variable `NASA_API_KEY` (placeholder name in `.env.example`).
- **Log all AI / "SI tool" use** in `docs/AI_USE.md` (date, tool, what for, what was kept or changed). The submission must describe this.
- **No photos, video, voices, or likenesses of under-18s** in the demo or submission. Prefer screen recording plus captions.
- **Cite data sources** and fetch dates. Do not invent facts. Mark unchecked items **UNVERIFIED**. The official Resources tab and judging guide arrive 13 November (**UNVERIFIED** until re-checked).
- Keep this repository **private**. Do not make it public and do not connect Vercel or other hosting/billing integrations.
- After 14 November: put raw downloads in gitignored `data/raw/`; write only small derived products to `data/processed/`; use a Mars radius (3,389.5 km mean, or 3,396.19 km equatorial from the DTM labels) for distances.
